            "description": "The node answers the error code **15** `CoordinatorNotAvailable` with the coordinator `-1:\"\":-1` and the empty message - not the 42 of every version below 6. `KafkaApis.getCoordinator` @ 3.9.2 passes the version gate and the `CLUSTER_ACTION` check and then returns that code out of the `CoordinatorType.SHARE` branch of its match, under the comment *\"When share coordinator support is implemented in KIP-932, a proper check will go here\"*: the share coordinator does not exist on a 3.9.2 node at all. The 15 is a **retriable** code for `Common\\CoordinatorLookup`, so a client that asked for this type would retry it until its timeout ran out - which is one more reason the share groups are out of this line.",
